{
  "category": "Uncategorized",
  "description": "Disable Leva Debug Panel in Production Build\n\nRemove the leva configuration panel that is incorrectly appearing in the production deployment at https://tnormington.github.io/habit-tracker/. The leva debug UI should only be visible during local development, not in deployed production environments.\n\nRequirements:\n- Identify where leva is being initialized or rendered in the codebase\n- Add environment check to conditionally render leva only in development mode\n- Verify NODE_ENV or equivalent environment variable is properly set in production builds\n- Ensure leva import is tree-shaken or excluded from production bundle\n- Test locally that leva appears in dev mode (npm run dev)\n- Verify leva does not appear after production build (npm run build && npm run start)\n- Deploy and confirm leva is hidden on GitHub Pages production URL\n- Consider moving leva initialization inside admin bar or dev tools section if not already there\n\nEdge Cases:\n- Check if leva CSS is still being loaded even when component is not rendered\n- Ensure no console errors occur when leva code is excluded\n- Verify any leva controls used in admin bar still function correctly in dev mode",
